# An example is a working project, so it accumulates build output. `files` in
# package.json allowlists this whole directory, and npm's usual exclusion of
# node_modules does not reach inside an allowlisted path — so without this,
# whatever a maintainer last built here ships to every user.
#
# The Dart sibling has had this file since the start. This package was created
# by mirroring that one's `files` list and not this, which is how 0.1.1 went out
# at 111 MB carrying a compiled .node binary. tool/prepack.js is the loud
# backstop; this is the quiet one.
node_modules/
build/
target/
Cargo.lock
package-lock.json
